From: djvalic <djvalic@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 11:47:47 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 14/16] ad5x: Keep U-Boot below the kernels' crash log

Kiln's kernels keep a ramoops region in the last MiB of the 236 MiB of
lowmem (0x0EB00000-0x0EBFFFFF), so that a panic's log survives the
reset. U-Boot relocated itself to the top of those 236 MiB, with its
16 MiB heap below, and overwrote it. Put the usable top of RAM at
0x0EB00000: relocation, heap and stack stay below the region.
---
 board/flashforge/ad5x/ad5x.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/flashforge/ad5x/ad5x.c b/board/flashforge/ad5x/ad5x.c
index 3e0178ca..42f12c81 100644
--- a/board/flashforge/ad5x/ad5x.c
+++ b/board/flashforge/ad5x/ad5x.c
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
  * Flashforge Adventurer 5X (Ingenic X2600)
  */
 
+#include <config.h>
 #include <blk.h>
 #include <command.h>
 #include <env.h>
@@ -39,6 +40,19 @@ int dram_init(void)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+/*
+ * The last MiB of those 236 holds the kernels' crash log (ramoops,
+ * 0x0EB00000-0x0EBFFFFF, kernel-ingenic66/ad5x.dts): U-Boot relocates
+ * itself, its heap and its stack below it, so a crash log survives into
+ * the next start.
+ */
+#define AD5X_RAMOOPS		0x0eb00000
+
+phys_addr_t board_get_usable_ram_top(phys_size_t total_size)
+{
+	return CFG_SYS_SDRAM_BASE + AD5X_RAMOOPS;
+}
+
 /*
